<Base
  title="About | CRISPR Screen Explorer"
  description="Why this project exists, who it is for, and how it is built."
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A hobby project to make large public CRISPR screen datasets usable by scientists who do not
    program, and to encourage standardized data use.
  </p>
  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Bench scientists and students who want to check a gene against public screens, and
    computational colleagues who want clean, citable, standardized data.
  </p>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every result links back to its source screen and publication.</li>
    <li>Licences and attribution are shown for every dataset.</li>
    <li>No accounts, no tracking cookies.</li>
    <li>Methods are written down so analyses can be reproduced.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="notice">This page will be expanded as the project develops.</p>
</Base>
